Adds a full chapter explaining the orthogonal-to-proxy layer that lives
in ~/.claude-copilot/ (user agent files + PreToolUse hook + settings.json
registration). Documents why naive `Explore.md` override only half-works
(model: opus alias falls back to built-in's hardcoded haiku for some
SDK code paths), and the clean 3-piece solution:

  1. Explore-copilot.md — parallel user agent with extracted Eb5 prompt,
     uses model: opus alias correctly (no name collision)
  2. redirect-explore-to-copilot.py — PreToolUse hook intercepting Agent
     tool calls AND Workflow tool script content, rewriting
     agentType:'Explore' → 'Explore-copilot' on both paths
  3. settings.json hooks.PreToolUse[matcher=Agent|Workflow] entry wiring
     the hook in

Verified on 2026-05-31: 100% opus dispatch, 0 HTTP 400 model_not_supported
errors, 0 SDK-internal haiku residual, workflow exit 0. Compared to the
override-only approach (16 opus + 2 haiku + 1 sonnet, 3 retry-swallowed
400s), the hook approach is fully clean.

Includes:
- The 4-layer evidence
- Why hook is preferred over binary patching (3 reasons: update churn,
  per-version brittleness, opacity)
- Full file reference layout
- Step-by-step extension pattern for future built-in agents that may
  similarly default to haiku
- Reversion path

This appendix is independent of the proxy patches (Patches 1 + 2);
keeping it separate so the layers stay decoupled in the reader's
mental model.
